\description{
A spatial data frame containing demographic, socioeconomic, and housing
characteristics for census tracts in the Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan area,
derived from the American Community Survey (ACS).
}
\details{
Data are derived from the American Community Survey (ACS), a continuous
survey conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau. Most variables represent 5-year
estimates aggregated at the census tract level, providing fine-grained
geographic detail suitable for neighborhood-level analysis within the
Dallas-Fort Worth metropolitan statistical area (DFW MSA).

Census tracts are designed to be relatively uniform in population size
(ideal range 1,200–8,000 residents) and represent stable neighborhoods with
recognizable geographic boundaries. This makes them more suitable than
counties for analyzing intra-metropolitan variation.

Percentage variables (prefix "PCT") are stored as numeric values between 0
and 100.

The \code{SchoolDistrict} and \code{Municipality} fields enable analysis of
educational access and local governance. The \code{CongLevel} variable
facilitates political and representative district analysis.
}
